      "alt": "Line chart titled \"Quality and decode speed on M4 Pro\" comparing model quality (mean score across 6 benchmarks, 0–100%) against decode speed (normalized AUC through 128K, tokens/s, 0–120).\nThe chart highlights a shaded region labeled \"Frontier gain from Flint\" between the \"Frontier without Flint\" baseline curve and the higher \"Frontier with Flint\" curve.\nKey data points plotted on the chart include:\n * Qwen3.8 27B near 85% score at ~8 tokens/s.\n * Flint llama.cpp (~47 tokens/s, ~81% score) and Flint MLX (~69 tokens/s, ~80% score), both represented as purple dots.\n * Qwen3.6 35B A3B and Qwen3.5 35B A3B around 70–72% score at ~37 tokens/s.\n * Baseline models plotted lower or further left, including Muse Glimmer 30B, Gemma 4 31B, Qwen3.5 9B, Qwen3.5 4B, and Laguna XS 2.1 33B A3B.\n * Faster, lower-scoring models at the bottom right include Qwen3.5 2B (~76 tokens/s, ~26% score) and Qwen3.5 0.8B (~110 tokens/s, ~15% score).\n",
